# NOTICE

Third-party content bundled with PhysLab, and the terms it is used under.

## Questions

PhysLab ships a small set of openly licensed practice questions from the Numbas open question bank
(numbas.mathcentre.ac.uk), gathered at build time within its authors' licence terms (S-Q QN1/QN2):
at most one request per second, the exact licence checked per item, and nothing PhysLab did not
already have a right to use. Only CC BY 4.0, CC BY-SA 4.0 and CC0 1.0 items are bundled; anything
else is refused. A picture PhysLab drew for a question that came with none is recorded below as a
"change", as CC BY and CC BY-SA both require saying when a work has been adapted.

Questions marked CC BY 4.0 are used under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence. Each names its author or source, who is credited here; the questions may be shared and adapted, with that credit kept, under the same or any other terms. Licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Questions marked CC BY-SA 4.0 are used under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence. Each names its author or source, who is credited here; an adapted version of such a question must carry the same licence. CC BY-SA 4.0 is one-way compatible with the GNU GPL version 3: a BY-SA question may be relicensed under GPLv3, but GPLv3 material may not come back under BY-SA. Licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Questions marked CC0 1.0 have been placed in the public domain by their authors under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal dedication. They may be used for any purpose without credit, though PhysLab names the source where one is known. Licence text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

